        "tree_id": "e0fc1eb29e4033bfc1ef140f205be74bd8e1ebd1",
        "message": "feat: protocol v2 — task ids, acks, replay protection, structured results; config management\n\nC2 reliability (implant + server + tests):\n- Server-generated task ids; tasks move queued -> sent -> acked -> done\n- At-least-once delivery: unacked tasks are re-served; implant dedups by\n  tid (last 32 seen) so retried tasks never execute twice; server\n  deduplicates retransmitted results (result_dup audit event)\n- Implant acks task receipt in the next beacon; server audit trail gains\n  task_queued/task_sent/task_ack/result/result_dup/replay_rejected\n- Monotonic counters inside the GCM-authenticated payloads on both\n  directions; non-advancing counters are rejected (replay protection),\n  re-baselined only on fresh handshakes / server restarts\n- Per-run implant id (8 hex) reported in beacons and results\n- Results carry machine-readable status: ok / error / timeout\n- tests/test_protocol.py grows to 27 checks covering all of the above\n\nConfiguration management (no hard-coded operational values):\n- Server: --config JSON file; precedence defaults < file < env < CLI;\n  result/audit caps, session TTL, queue depth, payload limit all tunable\n- Implant build: beacon token + min/max beacon interval are build-time\n  flags (GHOST_BEACON_TOKEN/_MIN/_MAX via build.sh prompts or env);\n  previous embedded token remains the fallback default\n\nDashboard (ui-ux-pro-max pass):\n- Results show task id + ok/timeout/error status badges; session detail\n  shows implant run id and sent/acked task counts\n- Focus-visible rings, prefers-reduced-motion support, status colors on\n  the existing OLED palette",
